https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=i7MLT4MmAK8  (Capo 2)

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (Gadd) and add the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  To emulate Enya's ethereal quality try strumming the chords not over the soundhole but over the fretboard where it joins the upper bout (14th or 12th fret).  Also strum very sparingly, perhaps even one strum per chord at the place indicated. 

TIP:  The words in the chorus, “Mornie utulie” (darkness has come) and “Mornie atlantie” (darkness has fallen) are not Gaelic but were created by J.R.R. Tolkein and are “Quenya Elfin,” the dialect spoken by the elves of Middle Earth.  Which of course is utter nonsense.  In order to sing them as Enya does they’re presented phonetically.
    

